.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev HA_TOKEN
Home Assistant long-lived access token. Required.
.It Ev OTEL_*
OpenTelemetry export (OTEL_SERVICE_NAME, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS,
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL).
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/creature/house.json
Configuration: the Home Assistant URL, the World URL, the house id, and the mappings from Home
Assistant entities to World subjects. A conffile; upgrades keep local edits.
.It Pa /etc/default/creature-house
Environment for the service, mode 0600. The only place
.Ev HA_TOKEN
lives.
.It Pa /var/lib/creature-house/
The outbox: events the World could not take yet, delivered when it is back.
.It Pa /usr/lib/systemd/system/creature-house.service
The unit. It runs as a
.Li DynamicUser
and is not started on install; set
.Ev HA_TOKEN ,
then
.Dl systemctl enable --now creature-house
.It Pa /usr/share/doc/creature-house/creature-house-manual.md
The operator's manual, including every configuration key and mapping kind.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl creature-house --config /etc/creature/house.json --log-level debug
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr creature-world 8 ,
.Xr creature-body 8
